sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch13-02> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The 'something more' than mere resemblance that naturalists seek in the Natural System is closeness of descent, which is the only known cause of similarity among organisms and is partially revealed by classifications.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Natural System expresses propinquity of descent";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter XIII, “Mutual Affinities of Organic Beings: Morphology: Embryology: Rudimentary Organs”; section “Natural system”. Scope: biological classification of all organisms"
}
